{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772643452,"nonce":"ywqABaXRTDJww8wLH2R666R0s/M=","title":"Typed subgraph taxonomy + pluggable canvas architecture","message":"Feedbax Studio currently has three distinct subgraph node types (Subgraph, PenzaiSubgraph, AcausalSystem) each implying different canvas editors, port semantics, and component palettes. This umbrella issue tracks the work to formalize this taxonomy and make the canvas/palette pluggable per subgraph type.\n\n## Subgraph types\n- **Subgraph** (causal): standard signal-flow graph, full palette\n- **PenzaiSubgraph** (Penzai): Penzai neural network modules, no editing in graph editor (issue c1ad986)\n- **AcausalSystem** (acausal/DAE): implicit equation solving, Mechanics/Control palette (issue a6efafc)\n\n## Key design questions\n1. When inside an AcausalSystem context, should a causal Subgraph be insertable? (Probably no — compatibility matrix needed)\n2. How should the canvas editor change when entering a PenzaiSubgraph vs AcausalSystem?\n3. Should pluggable canvas be data-driven (registry field: `canvas_editor_type`) or code-driven?\n\n## Related issues\n- c1ad986: NN internal uniformity \u0026 interpretability (Penzai core)\n- 7c0c4b2: Add Penzai-like selector API\n- a6efafc: DAE/Acausal subgraphs","files":null}]}